This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:

- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

The active firmware architecture is package-based and class-based:

- canonical board control headers live in `hardware/lib/board/*`
- canonical CAN headers live in `hardware/lib/can/*`
- canonical driver classes live in `hardware/lib/drivers/runtime/*` and `hardware/lib/drivers/mcp2515/*`
- canonical handler classes live in `hardware/lib/handlers/runtime/*` and `hardware/lib/handlers/variants/*`
- test-only helpers live in `hardware/test/support/*`
- feature packages live in `hardware/lib/packages/*`
- runtime contracts live in `hardware/lib/packages/runtime/*`
- nested FSD variant folders live in `hardware/lib/packages/fsd/legacy`, `hardware/lib/packages/fsd/hw3`, and `hardware/lib/packages/fsd/hw4`
- one package class per header inside each variant folder

When a change touches CAN-mutating logic, the minimum expected review bar is:

- exact bit-level regression coverage for the changed field
- short-frame/no-send coverage for every touched mutation path
- cross-check against `docs/CAN_CONTROL_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md`
